    "https://wingate.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Wingate-Campus/Student-Services-Coordinator--Julia-s-Learning_JR102208": {
      "title": "Student Services Coordinator, Julia's Learning",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWingate University is a teaching-focused institution serving more than 3,600 students across two campuses. Located on a beautiful 500+ acre main campus, Wingate offers a close-knit, supportive community where employees can grow, contribute, and thrive. As an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, Wingate is committed to fostering an inclusive environment and welcomes applicants who are excited to join our mission and make an impact. Learn more at  University in Charlotte, NC | Quick Facts About Wingate . The mission of Wingate University is to develop educated, ethical and productive global citizens. Following its Judeo-Christian heritage, the university seeks to cultivate the following in its students: Faith, Knowledge and Service.  The University’s Mission statement can be found here. Position Summary:   The Student Development &amp; Independent Living Specialist is a professional staff member responsible for designing and implementing the student development model for Julia’s Learning. Working as part of a three-person professional team, this position leads the Program’s efforts to help students build independence, executive functioning, social competence, self-advocacy, and adult living skills through individual coaching, experiential learning, and authentic campus and community experiences. This position serves as the program’s subject-matter expert in student development and transition to adulthood, partnering closely with the Director and Campus Support Coordinator to ensure students make meaningful progress toward individualized goals. Reports to: Director, Julia’s Learning Works collaboratively with: Campus Support Coordinator, student mentors, faculty, campus partners, families, and community organizations. Duties/Responsibilities :  Regular, predictable attendance on campus Alignment with University mission, vision, and strategic roadmap Student Development: Design and implement individualized student development plans; provide one-on-one coaching; help students develop executive functioning, problem-solving, decision-making, emotional regulation, communication, and self-advocacy skills. Independent Living: Develop learning experiences related to meal planning, cooking, apartment management, budgeting, transportation, personal wellness, organization, and daily routines. Curriculum & Program Development: Work alongside the Director in the development and continuous improvement of Julia’s Learning curriculum focused on college success, employment readiness, community engagement, and independent adulthood. Mentor Development: Train and coach student mentors to reinforce independence rather than create dependence; provide strategies for supporting neurodiverse learners. Assessment & Outcomes: Measure student growth, maintain progress documentation, recommend program improvements, and partner with the Director on individualized success plans. Campus & Community Integration: Create authentic learning opportunities through campus employment, student organizations, volunteerism, recreation, and community participation. Other job duties/responsibilities may be assigned. Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree preferred in occupational therapy rehabilitation counseling, special education, psychology, counseling, disability services, human development, recreation therapy, or a related field. Three or more years of experience supporting adolescents or young adults with intellectual and developmental disabilities, autism, or other neurodiverse populations. Demonstrated knowledge of executive functioning, transition-to-adulthood, independent living instruction, and person-centered planning. Experience developing curriculum, coaching individuals, and collaborating with multidisciplinary teams. Excellent interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Background in occupational therapy or OT-informed practice is highly desirable, but professional licensure is not required. Passion for higher education and inclusive college experiences. Innovative, collaborative, and strengths-based approach to student development. Ability to design systems and learning experiences that foster increasing independence. What Success Looks Like: Students demonstrate increasing independence across academic, residential, social, and employment settings. Student mentors consistently reinforce skill development. Julia’s Learning maintains a high-quality, evidence-informed student development model. Families and campus partners view the program as preparing students for successful adult lives. Benefits & Employee Experience: Wingate University is committed to supporting employees both personally and professionally through a comprehensive benefits package and a collaborative campus community. Full-time employees are eligible for medical, dental, and vision coverage; retirement plan with institutional contribution; paid time off and holidays; tuition benefits for employees and eligible dependents; and access to campus facilities, wellness resources, and professional development opportunities. Application Instructions: Thank you for your interest in joining the Wingate University community. Please complete all sections of the application and upload all required documents. A résumé is required for all positions, and a curriculum vitae (CV) is requested for faculty roles or other positions where applicable. Special Instructions: If a previous school, employer, or organization does not appear in the dropdown menu, please remove that section using the trash can icon and upload the relevant information in your application materials instead. This will insure your application moves forward without delay. In compliance with applicable law and University policies, Wingate University prohibits discrimination in its employment practices on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions, sexual orientation or gender identity), age, genetic information, disability and veteran status and encourages qualified candidates across all group demographics to apply.  At this time, we are currently seeking candidates with legal authorization to work in the U.S."
    },
    "https://wingate.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Wingate-Campus/Assistant-Professor--Management--Tenure-Track_JR102197": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor- Management, Tenure Track",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWingate University is a teaching-focused institution serving more than 3,600 students across two campuses. Located on a beautiful 500+ acre main campus, Wingate offers a close-knit, supportive community where employees can grow, contribute, and thrive. As an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, Wingate is committed to fostering an inclusive environment and welcomes applicants who are excited to join our mission and make an impact. Learn more at  University in Charlotte, NC | Quick Facts About Wingate . The mission of Wingate University is to develop educated, ethical and productive global citizens. Following its Judeo-Christian heritage, the university seeks to cultivate the following in its students: Faith, Knowledge and Service.   The University’s Mission statement can be found here. Position Summary: The Porter B. Byrum School of Business invites applications and nominations for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Management position at Wingate University. This opening is a full-time, 9-month faculty position reporting directly to the Dean of the Porter B. Byrum School of Business. The timeline to begin is August 2027. Duties and Responsibilities :  In addition to the duties listed below, faculty members must adhere to the general faculty guidelines as specified by Wingate University and perform other duties as assigned by the Dean of the Porter B. Byrum School of Business and the Provost. Teaching undergraduate (in person) and/or graduate (hybrid) courses in principles management, organizational behavior, and project management related courses face-to-face and hybrid. Conducting research leading to scholarly publication and engaging in service to the School of Business, University, profession and the community. Additional responsibilities as assigned by administrative personnel (Dean, Provost). Qualifications and Experience: Applicants must have a Ph.D. or DBA management with 18 graduate credit of hours in management from an accredited university, preferably AACSB accredited.  Professional experience is desirable. Candidates must have the ability to effectively teach courses in undergraduate and MBA . Candidates should demonstrate excellent teaching, strong communication skills, and provide evidence of being a subject matter expert through publishing scholarly work in peer- reviewed journals. Relevant experience in business and/or consulting--with a commitment to collaborative endeavors—is preferred. ABD candidates will be considered provided there is evidence that the doctorate degree will be completed within three years of appointment. Applicants with ABD status will be considered for the rank of Instructor until degree is completed . Required Documents: A letter of application with documented professional experience and reasons for interest in the position. Current curriculum vitae. Names and full contact information, including e-mail addresses of three (3) professional references. Unofficial transcripts. A brief statement of teaching philosophy, principles and vision regarding matters of campus inclusion. Official review of candidates will begin September 30th and continue until the position is filled.   Benefits & Employee Experience: Wingate University is committed to supporting employees both personally and professionally through a comprehensive benefits package and a collaborative campus community. Full-time employees are eligible for medical, dental, and vision coverage; retirement plan with institutional contribution; paid time off and holidays; tuition benefits for employees and eligible dependents; and access to campus facilities, wellness resources, and professional development opportunities. Application Instructions: Thank you for your interest in joining the Wingate University community. Please complete all sections of the application and upload all required documents. A résumé is required for all positions, and a curriculum vitae (CV) is requested for faculty roles or other positions where applicable. Special Instructions: If a previous school, employer, or organization does not appear in the dropdown menu, please remove that section using the trash can icon and upload the relevant information in your application materials instead. This will insure your application moves forward without delay. In compliance with applicable law and University policies, Wingate University prohibits discrimination in its employment practices on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions, sexual orientation or gender identity), age, genetic information, disability and veteran status and encourages qualified candidates across all group demographics to apply.  At this time, we are currently seeking candidates with legal authorization to work in the U.S."
    },
    "https://wingate.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Wingate-Campus/Wingate-Online--Adjunct-Faculty--Mathematics_JR102127": {
      "title": "Wingate Online- Adjunct Faculty, Mathematics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWingate University is a teaching university which serves more than 3,400 students on two campuses. Wingate is an equal employment opportunity employer.  Wingate’s main campus is located on 500+ acres of beautiful landscape and is only 25 minutes from the Charlotte, North Carolina metropolitan area. Learn more at  University in Charlotte, NC | Quick Facts About Wingate . Position Summary:   The Wingate University Online program seeks qualified adjunct instructors to teach online undergraduate math courses. Adjunct faculty play a vital role in delivering high-quality, accessible education to a diverse student population and are expected to maintain the academic standards and professional conduct consistent with the university's mission. Duties/Responsibilities :  Facilitate engaging, well-organized online courses in accordance with the course syllabus and Wingate Online guidelines Maintain a visible, responsive presence in the learning management system (LMS), including timely feedback on assignments and regular communication with students Post and adhere to grading turnaround times as established by the Office of Online Education Hold virtual office hours or provide equivalent availability for student support Uphold academic integrity policies and report violations as required Participate in required faculty orientations, trainings, Alignment with University mission, vision, and strategic roadmap Other job duties/responsibilities may be assigned Minimum Requirements: Master's degree in Mathematics or a closely related field required; a bachelor's degree with a minimum of five (5) years of relevant professional experience may be considered Specialization in one or more of the following areas: inferential statistics, quantitative reasoning, and/or data science Experience with online instruction and familiarity with LMS platforms (e.g., Canvas) Prior teaching experience at the college level preferred Demonstrated commitment to serving diverse student populations In addition to completing your application, please upload the following documents onto the application: current curriculum vitae, a letter of application with documented professional experience and reasons for interest in the position, names and full contact information including e-mail addresses for three professional references. The system will allow more than one document to be uploaded. Once your application has been submitted, you will not be able to upload any additional documents, or update any information on your application. In compliance with applicable law and University policies, Wingate University prohibits discrimination in its employment practices on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, age, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, genetic information, disability and veteran status and encourages qualified candidates across all group demographics to apply.  At this time, we are currently seeking candidates with legal authorization to work in the U.S."
